 sym:sym-sin[Sin] no more, lest a worse thing come upon you.”
 ____
 
-Notice that the penalty for sinning, also known as breaking the law after being healed, is worse than if we had never been healed or saved in the first place.
+Here sinning means breaking the law after being made well, and Jesus says that return leaves a man worse than before.
 This lines up exactly with what Hebrews said above: how much __“worse punishment”__ awaits the one who has trampled the Son of God underfoot (Hebrews 10:29).
 
 The most obvious way to willfully break the law of the LORD is to claim there is no law, it has been done away with, and that you do not have to follow it because __“Jesus has paid the price for you not following it”__.
